11. One more important issue: max_length=1024

You currently have:

max_length=1024

This is okay if your safety conversations fit within 1024 tokens.

But because you’re doing:

truncation=True

anything beyond 1024 gets silently truncated.

Before training, calculate how many examples exceed 1024.

For example:

lengths = []
for example in dataset["train"]:
    text = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(
        example["messages"],
        tokenize=False,
        add_generation_prompt=False,
    )
    lengths.append(len(tokenizer(text)["input_ids"]))
print("Max:", max(lengths))
print("Average:", sum(lengths)/len(lengths))
print("Over 1024:", sum(x > 1024 for x in lengths))

If only a small number exceed 1024, you’re fine.

If a large percentage exceed 1024, I’d consider 2048.

