My biggest concern with your current code

It’s actually this:

tokens["labels"] = tokens["input_ids"].copy()

I’d fix this before starting the actual training.

Because otherwise the model is being optimized to reproduce:

system message
+
user message
+
assistant response

instead of primarily learning:

assistant response

For your safety-understanding experiment, that can materially affect the quality of the fine-tuning.

So I would do this order:

1. Fix label masking ⭐
2. Remove device_map="auto"
3. Use BF16
4. Enable gradient checkpointing
5. Reduce LR from 2e-4 → 2e-5
6. Add 5% warmup
7. Enable load_best_model_at_end
8. Verify how many examples are truncated at 1024
9. Run a short sanity test before the full 3 epochs

